From: kraibse <33869366+kraibse@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:26:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: pack FP16 texture results with c0 in the low half

Ampere returns a TEX.F16 result as packed pairs, c0 in the low half of
the first destination. The lowering merges the two converted halves
with ISCADD, which shifts op_a up by 16, but gave op_a the low half:
H0 and H1 came out swapped. Ocarina of Time's tensor network reads blue
from .H0, so its image lost blue (gameplay blue mean 0.03 -> 0.60 with
EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=1).

Ported from Quixomatic/Eglantine dev ee247a0b68 (Franseven).

Co-authored-by: Franseven <spett2013@yahoo.it>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (found the fork commit, ported it, checked it in game)
(cherry picked from commit 29ed33831a3191ea620211dcd03570992f7fdffb)
---
 src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
index be1448aee2..b033267204 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
@@ -2442,7 +2442,9 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
                         if (target == 255) return;
                         emit(0x5ca8000000000000ULL | predicate | 246 | (u64{1} << 8) | (u64{2} << 10) | (u64{low} << 20));
                         emit(0x5ca8000000000000ULL | predicate | 247 | (u64{1} << 8) | (u64{2} << 10) | (u64{high} << 20));
-                        emit(0x5c18000000000000ULL | predicate | target | (u64{246} << 8) | (u64{247} << 20) | (u64{16} << 39));
+                        // ISCADD shifts op_a (bits 8..15) up, so op_a carries the high half and
+                        // op_b the low one; the other way round leaves H1 = c0 and H0 = c1.
+                        emit(0x5c18000000000000ULL | predicate | target | (u64{247} << 8) | (u64{246} << 20) | (u64{16} << 39));
                     };
                     pack(static_cast<u32>(dest), 250, components > 1 ? 251U : 255U);
                     if (components > 2) {
